---
title: Root vegetable tray bake
servings: 4
tags: [vegetarian, roast, autumn]
source: https://github.com/Gunde/recipes
---

Heat the #oven{} to 200 °C (180 °C fan).

Cut the @carrots{300%g} lengthways, and the @beetroot{300%g} and @celeriac{300%g} into wedges. Spread them in a #large roasting tin{}, drizzle with @olive oil{1%tbsp}, season with @salt{1%pinch} and @black pepper{1%pinch}, and roast for ~{20%minutes}.

Toss the @red onion{2}(cut into wedges) in @olive oil{1%tbsp} with a pinch of @salt{}. Add the onions and @thyme{2%sprigs} to the tin and roast for another ~{20%minutes}.

Meanwhile, make the sage and onion balls. Heat @olive oil{1%tbsp} and @butter{15%g} in a #frying pan{}, add the @onion{1}(large, finely chopped) and cook until soft and translucent. Stir in the @ground sage{1%tsp} and the zest of a @lemon{1}, then take the pan off the heat.

Tip the mixture into a bowl with the @breadcrumbs{150%g}, season well, and bind with the @egg{1}. Shape into eight balls.

Whisk together the @cider{150%ml}, @Dijon mustard{1%tsp}, @redcurrant jelly{1%tsp}, @yeast extract{1%tsp} and the hot @vegetable stock{150%ml}.

Take the tin out of the oven, scatter the @cannellini beans{400%g}(drained) over the vegetables and pour the sauce over everything.

Sit the balls on top and roast for a final ~{15-20%minutes}, until the balls are browned and cooked through and the sauce has reduced to a sticky glaze.

Serve with something green.
